# Repos a reviewer of THIS repo may search and cite, materialized under
# .siblings/<owner>/<repo>. Declared rather than left to the fallback so the
# set is the one this repo actually depends on.
#
# One per line. The reviewer host must also carry a SOURCE_PATHS entry for
# each, or the sibling reports as `missing` and is never searched.
#
# Each row is a real edge. `plow-openclaw-agent` is the base the Dockerfile
# builds FROM by digest, and `boot/` mirrors its boot step for step. `latch`
# owns the MCP tools and the gog grammar that every calendar, contact and
# iMessage read and write goes through. `plow-agents` owns the install
# contract the README follows.
#
# `agent-index-client` stays out: it reaches this repo only through the base.
# `plow-pbc/plow` is the server for every `/v1/...` call this repo makes, so a
# reviewer checks those calls against the real routes, not only against
# another client. It is private and this repo is public: cite it by
# `path:line`, don't quote its code.

plow-pbc/plow-openclaw-agent
plow-pbc/latch
plow-pbc/plow-agents
plow-pbc/plow
